WEBVTT

00:21:29.041 --> 00:21:30.823
and the future at the same time.

00:21:31.657 --> 00:21:35.977
So, when we look around, for example,
to digital space, the web,

00:21:35.977 --> 00:21:39.167
only a small fraction 
of the existing content

00:21:39.167 --> 00:21:42.487
is actually currently in Arabic,

00:21:42.487 --> 00:21:46.301
despite the continuing importance 
of the language,

00:21:46.301 --> 00:21:48.881
as we have just described.

00:21:48.881 --> 00:21:53.033
So, what does having 
curated content in Arabic

00:21:53.033 --> 00:21:57.293
through this new initiative 
TED (Arabic) mean to you?

00:21:57.293 --> 00:22:00.809
And what do you think it would mean
to Arabic speakers and thinkers